    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideStep1">Choose the game executable</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideBody1">Select the game&apos;s main EXE on Overview, such as the game client in its installation folder.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideStep2">Detect current settings</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideBody2">Run detection to view current settings and suggestions. Expand an item to learn what it does.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideStep3">Review before applying</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideBody3">Choose a few items at a time, review their effects and side effects, then apply the selection. Follow the elevation prompt when needed.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideStep4">Record the same scenario</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideBody4">Connect PresentMon and keep graphics settings, scene and sampling duration consistent when measuring before and after.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideStep5">Decide with an A/B comparison</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideBody5">Compare average FPS, 1% low and frame time across several runs. Consider stuttering and stability before keeping a setting.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideStep6">Review recovery scope</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Str.GuideBody6">Review saved settings in Backup and logs and choose the records to restore. Follow the record&apos;s guidance if a conflict appears.</s:String>
